   "id": "vibration-motor",
   "name": "Vibration motor (eccentric weight)",
   "description": "A little motor with an off-centre weight on its shaft (as in a phone or a game pad): powered (about 3 V, 80 mA) it spins at about 10 000 rpm and shakes whatever it's glued to. Small ones are fine on a pin through a transistor; straight on a pin is too much current.",
